- A relic is never lost to a stray delete, and never has to live in the code tree.
- The content format is open. A project decides what its specs, plans, decisions or transcripts contain.
- Parallel agents can update one relic without overwriting each other's text.
- Links between tasks, relics and parts are first-class and can be followed in both directions.
- Every change is kept, attributed, and comparable with any earlier version.
- Everything works from the command line with JSON output, with no service and no background process.
- Relic commands stay fast on large relics, and task commands do not get slower.
- A fresh clone can answer "what links to this?" within seconds.
